{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-05-i3-second-milestone-delivery.md at exact c404c8d8bca71c1beb0a11dc21c86c0ddcb5a52d on request/i3-m2, under promise git:sha1…92f987a on request git:sha1…575541e\n\nThe second I3 milestone alone, repaired, at c404c8d8bca71c1beb0a11dc21c86c0ddcb5a52d on request/i3-m2, for the planner's milestone request 53f83851. It replaces the filing at d0354e266 and answers verdict 25e00e2a (four P2) and the checker's documentation request 88503049, carried in this candidate. Primary subject: notes/2026-10-05-i3-second-milestone-delivery.md; its section 13 states the repairs, and section 26 of notes/2026-10-05-i3-contract-deltas.md (EZ1 to EZ11) records what was read and not changed, with owners. The source contradicted the verdict on no finding. Finding 1: a runner's report is read once into a canonical-safe value and never throws; a report not in form is a kept, signed report-malformed; twelve malformed reports give the same answer at the first delivery, a resend and a recovery, with one run. The report form is now exact, and its three bounds are the builder's numbers (EZ1). The sweep closed three more places where an outside party's reply was used before it was validated or could throw after a run was recorded: the lane's answer to the read-token request, the token driver reading a host reply twice, and a snapshot stored as given. Finding 2: a turn tells a listener after every transaction that moved the head, in commit order, and the object's listener is its existing follow step; a late answer's entry reaches a waiting stream with no call, no write and no stored alarm. Every entry is sealed by one function, so the one mechanism covers timed entries, deliveries, diagnoses, outcomes and late answers; the sweep also found that a checkpoint never followed anything, fixed by the same change. Limit: the stream is read inside the object's isolate, not over the route. Finding 3: the snapshot keeps an ID set beside the ordered objects; output digests taken from the earlier code are unchanged; work is counted as lookups, nothing is timed, and no bound is lowered. The sweep found and fixed two more quadratic loops in packages/platform/src/extents.ts, with answers pinned to the earlier code's digests. Finding 4: the read route serves the five kinds a commit stores by digest; a real read session, the Worker's route and the replay's own HTTP source read a retained snapshot from a real membership scope; the entry that stores it is made by hand through a real turn; a history with an ancestry record still replays as incomplete. The three guide corrections of request 88503049 are made, with four more of the same family. 22 controls were run and each distinguishes; seven did not at their first run and were rerun after the test was changed, as the note says. No form of an entry and neither lane digest changes. Gate: one observed run of npm run gate at 082efdf21 (tree 76ff797a), the merge of origin/main with milestone F landed, on the shared machine: typecheck 3.0 s, tests 9.6 s elapsed, 505 vitest tests in 67 files and 6 in Node's runner passed; the packages tree is 166c2676 at the gated commit and at this head; the one later commit changes the two notes. Against main: 175 paths added or changed and 42 deleted. The I3 commission bcf5ec17 and every remaining I3 duty stay open; nothing is deployed.","body":{"commit":"c404c8d8bca71c1beb0a11dc21c86c0ddcb5a52d","path":"notes/2026-10-05-i3-second-milestone-delivery.md"}}